🚽 Test case: `whopper` and `cringe` are ordinary identifiers.
🚽
🚽 Both used to be reserved words, and reserved for nothing: the lexer mapped
🚽 them to EXTERN and GOTO, but neither token appeared in any grammar
🚽 production -- only in lang.y's %token declaration. So the sole possible
🚽 effect of writing either one was a syntax error, in both roles:
🚽
🚽     whopper rizz counter;   -> syntax error, unexpected EXTERN
🚽     rizz whopper = 5;       -> syntax error, unexpected EXTERN
🚽
🚽 They cost a usable name and delivered nothing.
🚽
🚽 ── Why neither is coming back ────────────────────────────────────────
🚽 `extern` exists in C to tell one translation unit that a symbol lives in
🚽 another, for the linker to resolve. Brainrot has no separate compilation:
🚽 #cooked splices source, so a function defined in another file simply
🚽 resolves with no declaration of any kind, and a native module registers
🚽 its functions at load. There is no forward-declaration problem to solve
🚽 and no linker to inform -- the same structural argument that makes
🚽 include guards unnecessary.
🚽
🚽 `goto` is a different case and was removed for a different reason: it is
🚽 meaningful, just unwanted. It was never implemented, and the decision is
🚽 that it will not be.
🚽
🚽 ── What this fixture pins ────────────────────────────────────────────
🚽 That both names work in every position an identifier can appear, since
🚽 the lexer does not distinguish them: a function name, a parameter, a
🚽 struct field, and a local. Re-adding either lexer rule turns all four
🚽 into parse errors, so this fails loudly rather than subtly.
🚽
🚽 The functions are CALLED, not just declared -- an earlier draft declared
🚽 them and then shadowed both names with locals before ever using them, so
🚽 the "function name" claim was unbacked.
🚽
🚽 The struct field matters slightly more than it looks -- field names go
🚽 through the same IDENTIFIER token, so a reserved word breaks a data
🚽 layout and not just a variable.
gang Meal {
    rizz whopper;
    rizz cringe;
};

rizz cringe(rizz n) {
    bussin n + 1;
}

rizz whopper(rizz cringe) {
    🚽 A PARAMETER named after the other freed word. Also proves the two are
    🚽 independent: nothing here knows `cringe` is also a function name.
    bussin cringe * 2;
}

skibidi main {
    🚽 Called before any local shadows them, so both function names are
    🚽 genuinely exercised rather than merely declared.
    yapping("functions %d %d", cringe(41), whopper(21));

    gang Meal m;
    m.whopper = 2;
    m.cringe = 3;
    yapping("fields    %d %d", m.whopper, m.cringe);

    rizz whopper = 5;
    rizz cringe = 7;
    yapping("locals    %d %d", whopper, cringe);

    bussin 0;
}
